'''Le'Prude''' (アカンゾウ, ''Akanzou'') is a [[:Category:Red Enemies|Red]] variant of [[Le'boin]] that appears in [[Zero Legends]]. They were introduced in [[Version 15.2 Update|Version 15.2]].

{{Enemy Info
|name = Le'Prude
|image = E 768.png
|first appearance = '''ZL:''' [[Synthol Swamp|Sub-chapter 29 - Synthol Swamp]]
|money drop = 1,500¢ - 5,925¢
}}

==Enemy==
Le'Prude has enormous bulk and a comparatively faster attack rate to most other non-event-exclusive Le'boin variants. Their lower damage is made up for by a combination of 400 range [[Omni Strike]] and guaranteed [[Explosion]]s, giving them phenomenal reach which allows them to hit all the way up to 675 range and easily advance due to low standing range of 250. This, as well as the lingering hitboxes of Explosions, makes for a potent pusher who can easily repel fragile units like [[Slime Cat (Rare Cat)|Jelly Dumpling Cat]]. In addition, Le'Prude's [[Immune to Freeze|Immunity to Freeze]] renders it impossible to stop them from attacking, particularly countering the likes of [[Apple Cat (Super Rare Cat)|iCat]] or [[Celestial Child Luna (Uber Rare Cat)|Salvation's Daughter Lunacia]].

==Strategy==
Le'Prude's relatively fast attacks and lingering hitboxes from Explosions make it nearly impossible to approach them with units that have lacking health or survivability, notably making [[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]] a risky choice. Units that can tank the hits without being knocked back, such as those with [[Strong]], [[Resistant]] or [[Insanely Tough]] against Red, are more effective; some such units include [[Talents|Talented]] [[Dom Cat (Special Cat)|Dark Lazer]], [[Fish Cat (Normal Cat)|Island Cat]], [[Crazed Fish Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Island Cat]], and [[Sushi Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Roe Cat]], the latter of which can also Weaken Le'Prude to neutralize their damage.

Also keep in mind that while Le'Prude's base health and damage aren't incredibly high, they're buffed to 200% in [[Zero Legends]], giving them a whopping '''2.8 ''million''''' health and 21,600 damage. As such, taking them out will not be easy and they are nearly impossible to rush down in any way, shape, or form. This also means that Le'Prude can serve as both an attacker and a tank for ranged enemies, therefore, depending on the enemies that accompany Le'Prude, you may need high pierce from [[:Category:Long Distance Cats|Long Distance]]/[[:Category:Omni Strike Cats|Omni Strike]]/[[:Category:Wave Attack Cats|Wave]]/[[:Category:Surge Attack Cats|Surge]]/[[:Category:Explosion Cats|Explosion]] units to nullify their tanking potential.

