==Trivia==
*A prude is someone opposed to or sensitive to anything naughty. It also happens to contain the word ''rud'' (redness; to redden).
*Le'Prude's Japanese name, アカンゾウ ''Akanzou'', may be derived from 赤 ''aka'' (red), あかん ''akan'' (a [[wikipedia:Kansai dialect|Kansai]] term for "unacceptable", "forbidden", "not allowed" or "no good"), 簡素 ''kanso'' (simple/plain, referencing Le'Prude's minimal design changes from [[Le'boin]]), 感想 ''kansō'' (impressions, thoughts or reactions), ぞ ''zo'' (a masculine sentence-ending particle that indicates emphasis, sometimes for a warning or threat) and 像 ''zō'' (elephant).
*Le'Prude may have been inspired by the [https://youtu.be/xRwIykRc5Dw red elephants] of [[wikipedia:Tsavo|Tsavo]], Kenya, whose skin gains a red hue from the iron-oxide-rich soil that accumulates on them. These distinctive elephants are one of the most iconic features of [https://www.britannica.com/place/Tsavo-National-Park Tsavo National Park].
*Le'Prude is the first non-event enemy since [[Le'noir]] (from [[Version 3.5 Update|Version 3.5]]) whose design is purely a recolor of another enemy.
**Incidentally, both are variants of Le'boin.

